---
/** Why, cases 5 to 7: the browser FiveM embeds, an app in LB Phone, and working without the game. */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Case from './Case.astro';
import Code from '../Code.astro';
import Terminal from '../Terminal.astro';
import devLog from '../../assets/shots/dev-log.png';
import devPhone from '../../assets/shots/dev-phone.png';
import { href } from '../../lib/paths';
import * as sample from '../../samples/why-tooling';

const WIDTHS = [640, 960, 1280, 1920];
const SIZES = '(min-width: 1264px) 1136px, calc(100vw - 42px)';
---

<Case
  id="why-chromium"
  index={5}
  title="It works in Chrome and fails in game"
  todayEnds="Nothing warns you in the browser you develop in. In game the layout is wrong, or the script throws."
  nexusEnds="Refused by the check and by the build, with what to write instead."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    FiveM's browser is Chromium 103. CSS it does not know is silently ignored there, and a missing JavaScript function throws, while
    both work in the browser you develop in. Newer syntax is not a problem: the build rewrites it.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="today">
    <Code code={sample.modernCss} lang="css" file="web/style.css" tone="bad" marks={[{ text: 'color-mix', tone: 'bad' }, { text: ':has', tone: 'bad' }]} />
    <Code code={sample.modernJs} lang="js" file="web/app.js" tone="bad" marks={[{ text: 'toSorted', tone: 'bad' }]} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="nexus">
    <Code code={sample.fixed} lang="nexus" file="web/screens/Shop.nexus" tone="good" lines={{ 6: 'good', 10: 'good', 16: 'good', 19: 'good' }} />
    <Terminal output={sample.fixedCheck} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="result">
    <Terminal output={sample.compatCheck} title="What the check said about the first version" />
    <p class="case-note">
      The list of what is caught, and what is not, is in
      <a href={href('/docs/format/#what-chromium-103-cannot-run')}>the format reference</a> and the
      <a href={href('/docs/roadmap/')}>roadmap</a>: new DOM methods are only caught from a fixed list.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</Case>

<Case
  id="why-phone"
  index={6}
  title="A phone app is a second build and a second bridge"
  todayEnds="Two pages to build, two ways to send a message, and registration to keep alive by hand."
  nexusEnds="The same build and the same contract. On a server without LB Phone the line does nothing."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    A screen with <code class="ic">surface="phone"</code> or <code class="ic">surface="tablet"</code> is an app in LB Phone or LB
    Tablet. Calls, pushes, state and strings work in it as in any screen.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="today">
    <Code code={sample.phoneLua} lang="lua" file="client/phone.lua" tone="bad" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="nexus">
    <Code code={sample.phoneScreen} lang="nexus" file="web/screens/ShopApp.nexus" tone="good" lines={{ 7: 'good' }} />
    <Code code={sample.phoneApp} lang="lua" file="client/main.lua" tone="good" lines={{ 1: 'good' }} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="result">
    <figure class="case-shot">
      <Image src={devPhone} alt="The garage example in a browser, with its LB Phone app shown in a phone frame over the garage screen" widths={WIDTHS} sizes={SIZES} loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>The example resource under <code>nexus dev</code>: its phone app in a frame of the size LB gives it, fed by the same mock.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>
</Case>

<Case
  id="why-dev"
  index={7}
  title="Every change needs the game"
  todayEnds="A restart and a walk back to the menu for every change."
  nexusEnds="Save the file. The open screen is mounted again in place, with the props it had."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    <code class="ic">nexus dev</code> runs the page in a browser with a mock in place of the game. The mock enforces the contract
    exactly as the Lua side does, with the same codes and the same messages. The game is needed to test the Lua.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="today">
    <Code code={sample.gameLoop} lang="sh" file="the loop" tone="bad" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="nexus">
    <Terminal output={sample.devLoop} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="result">
    <figure class="case-shot">
      <Image src={devLog} alt="The garage example in a browser under nexus dev: the garage screen, a vehicle HUD, the toolbar, and the bridge log listing calls with their answers and refusals" widths={WIDTHS} sizes={SIZES} loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>
        The toolbar opens screens with the props from the mock. The log shows what crossed the bridge: an accepted purchase, one
        the handler refused, and one the contract refused.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>
</Case>
